---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description="How this site earns money, and why it cannot affect the rankings.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p>
      Links from {site.name} to retailers may be affiliate links. If you buy after following one, the retailer may pay
      us a commission. It costs you nothing extra.
    </p>
    <h2>It does not affect the ranking</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Tables are ordered purely by price per dose, calculated the same way for every product.</li>
      <li>Retailers and brands cannot pay for placement, and there are no sponsored or “featured” rows.</li>
      <li>Retailers that pay no commission are ranked exactly the same way as those that do.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Amazon</h2>
    <p>
      As an Amazon Associate, {site.name} earns from qualifying purchases. “Check on Amazon” links are searches, not
      price comparisons: Amazon’s prices are not yet in our tables, so a product may be cheaper or dearer there. When
      Amazon’s product data is available to us, Amazon will appear as ordinary rows ranked by price like every other
      retailer.
    </p>
    <p>The full method is on the <a href="/methodology/">how we compare</a> page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
